course: dictionary
lesson: 3579
title: Fewer and fewest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Use fewer when you are counting things, such as apples, mistakes or people. «Habits change slowly: fewer bad influences and more good things to do help.» Bad influences can be counted one by one, so fewer is the right word.
explain: To find how many fewer one group has, subtract. If Ava has 9 marbles and Tom has 6, Tom has 9 − 6 = 3 fewer marbles than Ava. "How many fewer" always asks for the difference.
explain: Few means not many. Fewest means the smallest number of all: if Mia has 2 cards, Sam has 5 and Ravi has 8, Mia has the fewest. "No fewer than" means at least: "no fewer than 20 people" means 20 or more.
fact: Fewer is used for things you can count, such as fewer apples or fewer pencils.
fact: Few means not many, and fewest means the smallest number of all.
fact: To find how many fewer, subtract the smaller number from the bigger number.
fact: «Fewer than» compares two amounts, and «no fewer than» means at least.
exercise: Ava has 9 marbles and Tom has 6. How many fewer marbles does Tom have than Ava? | *3 | 15 | 5 | 2
exercise: Choose the right word: There are ___ biscuits in the tin than yesterday. | less | fewest | more | *fewer
exercise: Mia had 2 cards, Sam had 5 and Ravi had 8. Who has the fewest cards? | Ravi | Sam | Nobody | *Mia
test: Ella has 12 sweets and Jack has 7. How many fewer sweets does Jack have than Ella? | 6 | 7 | *5 | 4
test: Which sentence is correct? | The shop has less apples. | *The shop has fewer apples. | The shop has few apple. | The shop has fewest apple.
exam: «There were no fewer than 20 people at the match.» What does no fewer than mean? | *20 or more | Exactly 5 | 20 or fewer | Fewer than 2
